  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SECURING SHOREBIRD SITES AT MAULLIN, CHILE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To reduce the loss and degradation of habitat from unregulated recreational activities and livestock disturbance in one of the largest coastal wetlands in continental Chile, the project will: 1) work toward the establishment of a 970-hectare municipal protected area network that provides feeding and resting habitat for Hudsonian Godwit and other shorebirds; 2) develop a management plan for the protected area network; 3) monitor bird numbers and habitat usage, threats, and reserve management outcomes; 4) assist local communities in developing ecotourism and in understanding the importance of the protected areas; 5) create bird observation platforms, signage, radio broadcasts and printed and online information materials.</narrative>
  </description>
